  "Question": "If walking 5 m east is recorded as +5 m, what does -3 m represent? (Choose the correct answer.)",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Walking 3 m east",
    "B": "Walking 5 m west",
    "C": "Walking 5 m east",
    "D": "Walking 3 m west"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Positive and negative signs represent opposite directions. If east is positive, a negative sign represents west. The value 3 indicates a distance of 3 m, so it means walking 3 m west.",
